====Verb====
{{en-verb|fugg}}

# {{euphemistic form of|fuck|lang=en}}
## {{non-gloss definition| Used to express displeasure. }}
##* {{quote-book|year=1948 |title=Naked Dead |author=Norman Mailer  |page=692 |passage=He knew he would never eat them; they were merely an added load in his pack. Aaah, '''fug''' this. }}
##* {{quote-book|year=1969 |title=Blues Chased a Rabbit |author=Seymour Blicker - |page=62 |passage=Scornfully the driver answered, "'''Fug''' you muthafug, you ain't gon drive this muthafuggin cah."  }}
##* {{quote-book|year=2005 |title=The World's Thinnest Fat Man: Stories |author=Joe Taylor |page=82 |ISBN=0930501225 |passage="'''Fug''' this place," Jeff said. "Let's go to the pier in case that jerk comes back with a gun." }}
## To [[damage]] or [[destroy]].
##* {{quote-book|year=2007 |title=Dodging the Bull: Stories |author=Paul Mitchell |page=51 |ISBN=1862547491 |passage=Zit my fault the rotary '''fugged''' up and the new one's buggered? }}
##* {{quote-book|year=2010 |title=Metroland |author=Julian Barnes |page=39 |ISBN=140908874X |passage=You mean like in Zola–because they were '''fugged''' up in their turn by their parents. }}
##* {{quote-book|year=2013 |title=The Apprentice Journals |author=J. Michael Shell |page=7 |ISBN=1907133380 |passage=Tell them every detail, so they can find an Apprentice again, because if they don't, they're '''fugged'''.” }}
##* {{quote-book|year=2013 |title=Want Not |author=Jonathan Miles |page=33 |ISBN=0544114639 |passage=He did an imitation of Big Jerry in full-choke cantankerousness: “'You'll just '''fug''' it up.'  }}
## To [[copulate]] with.
##* {{quote-book|year=2014 |title=Urban Spacemen & Wayfaring Strangers |author=Richie Unterberger |page= |ISBN=0991589246 |passage= All went well until girls started writing things like, 'I want to win a date with Tuli because I want him to '''fug''' me.' }}
##* {{quote-book|year=2016 |title=Metroland  |author=Julian Barnes |page=10 |ISBN=1784705918 |passage=Married, two children, doesn't let him '''fug''' her any more.  }}

